/*! \page page_cutils AnCH CUtils library documentation
 *
 * \tableofcontents
 *
 * \section cutils_intro_seq Introduction
 *
 * AnCH CUtils library provides a gateway between C and C++: C++ streams over C style read and write functions.
 *
 * \section cutils_prereq_sec Prerequisites
 *
 * AnCH CUtils is a standalone library.
 *
 * \section cutils_install_sec Installation
 *
 * CMake target \c anch::cutils:
 * \code{.cmake}
find_package(Anch REQUIRED)
target_link_libraries(my-app PRIVATE anch::cutils)
\endcode
 * See \ref install_sec "installation".
 *
 * \section cutils_concept_sec Conception
 *
 * An \ref anch::cutils::cbuffer "cbuffer" describes a buffer size and C style \c read and \c write functions
 * (they return the number of bytes read or written ; \c read returns \c 0 at end of data).
 * \ref anch::cutils::CIStream "CIStream", \ref anch::cutils::COStream "COStream" and
 * \ref anch::cutils::CIOStream "CIOStream" are standard streams over them: partial writes are retried and
 * write errors set the stream bad bit. anch-network sockets are built on them.
 *
 * \section cutils_example_sec Examples
 *
 * \snippet{trimleft} anch-cutils/examples/cutils.cpp example
 */
